<title>UK: German inland gas oil drops, demand stays firm.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil drops, demand stays firm.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.7276)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     33.30/33.50     19.28/19.39   33.70/34.00</p>
<p> BREMEN		33.30/33.50     19.28/19.39   33.70/34.00</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    33.10/33.30     19.16/19.28   33.50/33.80</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   33.70/34.00     19.51/19.68   34.00/34.40</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   33.80/34.10     19.56/19.73   34.30/34.60</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  34.80/35.20     20.14/20.38   35.00/35.40</p>
<p>German inland gas oil dropped on Wednesday in line with easier gas oil futures. Traders said the buying interest seen earlier in the week was now translating into deals.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 8980</p>
</text>
